cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Shift-stable exponents and congruences for exponential generating functions
  (Lean 4 formalization)
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Turazashvili"
    given-names: "Nikoloz"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of a congruence theorem for sequences
  b(n) = n! [x^n] (W(x) F(x)^A(n) exp(x G(x)^M(n))) with F(0) = G(0) = 1, an
  unconstrained prefactor W, and shift-stable exponent functions A, M. The
  theorem resolves conjectures of Peter Bala on OEIS sequences A361036,
  A361281, A293013 and the general conjecture on A278070, and subsumes Bala's
  2017 theorem.
keywords:
  - number theory
  - integer sequences
  - congruences
  - exponential generating functions
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - OEIS
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/turazashvili/shift-stable-exponents"
